goucl — provenance and attribution
==================================

goucl is a port of libucl, the C reference implementation of the Universal
Configuration Language, together with a compatibility layer reproducing the
API of the cgo binding github.com/mitchellh/go-libucl.

Almost none of this library is original work. What follows records where each
part came from, so that credit lands where it belongs and so that anyone
redistributing goucl can satisfy the upstream licence terms.


How the code was produced
-------------------------

The Go in internal/core was produced by automated translation of libucl's C
sources by a large language model, function by function, rather than written
from a specification or by hand. The translation is deliberately literal:
Go functions carry the names of the C functions they came from, the control
flow follows the original, and the reference notes in docs/reference/ record
the C behaviour each file was translated against.

Correctness is not claimed on the strength of the translation. It rests on
differential testing against the compiled C library: 168 golden outputs
captured from libucl across six emitter modes, libucl's own test corpus, and
targeted probes built against libucl.a whenever the Go and the C appeared to
disagree. Places where this port knowingly departs from the C, and why, are
listed in docs/findings.md.


