The whole of internal/core is a translation of libucl's C sources:

    src/ucl_parser.c ............ internal/core/parser.go, parse_value.go
    src/ucl_util.c .............. internal/core/object.go, parser_macro.go,
                                  convert.go, compat.go
    src/ucl_emitter.c ........... internal/core/emit.go
    src/ucl_emitter_streamline.c  internal/core/emit_stream.go
    src/ucl_emitter_utils.c ..... internal/core/emit.go
    src/ucl_hash.c .............. internal/core/hash.go (behaviour only; see
                                  "Not derived from" below)
    src/ucl_msgpack.c ........... internal/core/msgpack*.go
    src/ucl_schema.c ............ internal/core/schema.go
    src/ucl_sexp.c .............. internal/core/sexp.go
    src/ucl_chartable.h ......... internal/core/parse_value.go
    include/ucl.h ............... internal/core/types.go, parser.go

Test fixtures under internal/core/testdata/ are copied verbatim from the
libucl distribution. The golden outputs beside them were generated by running
the compiled C library over those fixtures.

